      summary:
        "This law makes free, compulsory schooling a legal right for every child aged 6 to 14 in India, so no government school can charge fees or turn away a child in this age group. It also requires private, unaided schools to reserve at least 25% of entry-level seats for children from disadvantaged and economically weaker sections, with the government reimbursing the school's cost. Schools must also meet minimum standards for classrooms, teachers, and facilities.",
