      summary:
        'This law created a business structure called an LLP that combines the flexibility of a traditional partnership with limited liability protection, meaning partners are not personally responsible for the LLP\'s debts beyond what they invested. It is a popular choice for small businesses, professional firms (like CA or law firms), and startups that want partnership-style management without the risk of losing personal assets if the business runs into debt. LLPs must be registered with the Ministry of Corporate Affairs and file annual returns.',
