      summary:
        "This law sets the ground rules whenever goods (physical products, not services or property) are bought and sold in India. It defines the seller's duty to deliver goods that match what was promised in quality and description, the buyer's right to reject goods that don't match, and who bears the loss if goods are damaged before delivery. Today it works alongside the Consumer Protection Act, giving buyers extra legal backing when goods turn out to be defective or not as described.",
