        summary: 'Consolidates 29 central labour laws into four codes: the Code on Wages, the Industrial Relations Code, the Code on Social Security, and the Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Code. Introduces a uniform definition of wages under which basic pay must be at least 50% of total compensation, which changes how provident fund and gratuity amounts are calculated, and standardises digital compliance for employers. Formally notified and enforced from 21 November 2025, with state-level rules rolling out through April 2026.',
