        summary: 'An Andhra Pradesh state law enacted to curb the widespread practice of forcibly or fraudulently occupying land belonging to the government, religious/charitable institutions, or private persons. It declares land grabbing unlawful, provides for the constitution of Special Courts or Tribunals to swiftly investigate and adjudicate grabbing disputes, and empowers these courts to order eviction, restitution, and criminal punishment of land grabbers. Any sale, lease, or other transfer of grabbed land made without the Special Court\'s sanction is treated as null and void. Applies only within Andhra Pradesh.',
