        summary:
          'This law imposed a complete ban on the manufacture, sale, possession, transport, and consumption of alcohol across Bihar, replacing an earlier 2015 prohibition law after courts struck down some of its harsher provisions. Anyone caught with liquor can face arrest and prosecution, and in its original form the law allowed collective fines on entire villages or households and made even first-time consumption punishable with jail, though the Supreme Court later required individualised evidence rather than automatic collective punishment. The law has been credited with reducing some alcohol-related domestic violence, but has also led to a large illegal liquor trade, overcrowded prisons from prohibition-related arrests, and repeated hooch-tragedy poisoning deaths.',
